{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert the judgment of your poor man in his dispute.</b> In order to find him liable in judgment. This is a warning to the judge, even though it did not mention him. Like 'before YHWH your Elohim you shall eat it' (Deut. 15:20), which is stated regarding the firstborn, which belongs only to the priest. Above (v. 3) it warned not to tilt in favor of the poor man out of pity, and here it warns not to tilt against him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:59.856077134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}